In your opionion, what are the 5 most important parameters available when submitting a job and why? 

#SBATCH --nodes=2    --> This selects the number of nodes you want to use

#SBATCH --ntasks-per-node=2     --> This sets the tasks per node

#SBATCH --exclusive     --> If you omit this, you cannot chose the cores freely on the node, 
                            they will be assigned to you!

#SBATCH --nodelist n001   --> Not SO important but useful if you want to select specific nodes

#SBATCH --array=1-5   --> If you want to run the job multiple time for reduncdance
#SBATCH --output=osu-%A_%a.out    # %A = array job ID, %a = index


What are possible settings of these parameters, and what effect do they have?
#SBATCH --nodes=2   --> Natural Number (in our case 1-14)
#SBATCH --ntasks-per-node=2   --> Natural Number (in our case 1-6)
#SBATCH --exclusive   --> No parameters, if set, you have the full node to yourself
#SBATCH --nodelist n001  --> n00[1-14], select specific nodes
#SBATCH --array=1-5 --> Range with natural Numbers, set number of repititions
#SBATCH --output=osu-%A_%a.out --> Sting with special characters, the name of the output file

How do you run your program in parallel? What environment setup is required?

-> Just run it, if it supports multiple processes in parallel, you yourself need to enable that.

-> No special environment is required, just run it on any system supporting
multiple processes in parallel. However, if you want to run it on a cluster like lcc3,
you need to submit a slurm job to get the resources needed to run your program. But apart from 
the allocation, you are free to go.

